From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] llama : use the llama-bpe pre-tokenizer for BitNet b1.58 2B-4T

microsoft/BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf has no tokenizer.ggml.pre, so llama.cpp
falls back to the "default" pre-tokenizer and warns that generation quality
will be degraded. The original model (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T) uses the
Llama 3 tokenizer. The two split text differently: for example "I'm",
"they'll", "won't" and blank lines give different tokens.

When the architecture is bitnet-b1.58 and tokenizer.ggml.pre is missing, use
"llama-bpe". A file that sets tokenizer.ggml.pre, or --override-kv
tokenizer.ggml.pre=..., is not affected.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

diff --git a/src/llama-vocab.cpp b/src/llama-vocab.cpp
index 2b546c4..ae1ab82 100644
--- a/src/llama-vocab.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-vocab.cpp
@@ -2108,6 +2108,12 @@ void llama_vocab::impl::load(llama_model_loader & ml, const LLM_KV & kv) {
             add_space_prefix = false;
             escape_whitespaces = false;
             clean_spaces = true;
+            // microsoft/BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf has no tokenizer.ggml.pre; the
+            // original model (microsoft/bitnet-b1.58-2B-4T) uses the Llama 3 tokenizer.
+            if (tokenizer_pre.empty() && kv.arch == LLM_ARCH_BITNET_B158) {
+                LLAMA_LOG_INFO("%s: missing pre-tokenizer type for bitnet-b1.58, using: 'llama-bpe'\n", __func__);
+                tokenizer_pre = "llama-bpe";
+            }
             if (tokenizer_pre.empty()) {
                 LLAMA_LOG_WARN("%s: missing pre-tokenizer type, using: 'default'\n", __func__);
                 LLAMA_LOG_WARN("%s:                                             \n", __func__);
